Z||000000||speed racer||07-20-2000||05:26 PM||||If the check engine light is not on does that mean that all the codes are right?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-20-2000||06:37 PM||||Not necesarily so.  Some times the code gets tripped, but the light may not go on. You need to read the codes stored. <BR>When the light goes Blink.....Blink, Blink,  there are no codes stored.  Unless the bulb is burned out.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||07-20-2000||11:50 PM||||If the condition that set the code clears up, the code will remain in memory until there are 50 engine start without the code reappearing. The light goes on while the error condition is active.||||reg||1
